d a throw voids the sweep — `check` does not return, and re-threading the previous waitset re-polls every entry, re-appending writers that already appended (`check` docstring) | Faithful to the engine. Catching around host resolver composition would hide host defects inside a diagnostic the library cannot ground; the no-dropped-state law is documented as the resolvers' obligation instead (W1 review, P2) |\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:246:  Outcome: no P0-P2; verdict \"ready to commit\". One P3 applied in the same\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:449:  the convention in the plan now so P2's pool observer needs no retrofit.\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:468:    50d48a71-9ff9-44b7-8dc0-b334e5f42aac | ready to commit, no P0-P2, three\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:545:    ready to commit\"; one P2 (the deletion/cleanup gap); confirmed the new\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:572:Next: **P2** — the pool, its two ends, and the in-memory backend — is the next\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:585:**P2 and P3 of docs/design/dao.jing.implementation-plan.md**, delegated and verified.\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:586:`glm-5.3` completed P2: rebuilding `dao.jing`'s observer over `dao.stream.observe/step`, migrating the pool's writer seams to v2, and successfully migrating all nine test files to v2 streams and ringbuffers. The Clj and Cljs test suites passed cleanly under the delegate, and `bb test:cljd` was verified separately on the host with 0 failures.\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:590:`gpt-5.6-sol` performed the routine cross-family code review on the full P2 implementation diff. It identified two P1 testing gaps (three test drains were stopping silently on gap/defect signals rather than failing) and one P2 documentation contradiction in `dao.jing.md`. All findings were fixed directly.\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:592:The work for P2 and P3 is now complete, verified, and ready to commit.\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:716:- P2 (the `dao.space.query.md` rewrite) not started.\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:780:- P2 (the `dao.spa