ferential harness test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj — A-leg runs UPSTREAM latte on the host, C-leg compiles the same source via yang.clojure and runs on the VM; blocked-feature classifier (loop/recur, destructuring, case, stdlib symbols, docstrings, multi-arity) predicts C-leg blockers; FIRST END-TO-END ORACLE PASS: defenv/mkenv A=[[] {}] == C=[[] {}]; vectorn? correctly recorded blocked (unresolved host symbols). SLICE 2: compile-if no longer swallows an explicit false alternate (alt-present? arity, the architect-found bug); literal semantics changed per architect ruling — constant-form? added, collections with dynamic elements lower to conj/assoc calls (elements evaluate), nested quotes route through compile-form (reviewer P2 fix), quoted/constant collections stay literal. Consumer migration: 5 macro_test sites (c '[x]) -> (c '(quote [x])) — verified green-at-HEAD via stash before attributing.\\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:14117:Decisions: Owner corrected the seat twice: (1) architect designs before implementing (done, collab/1793128583916), (2) remember the orchestrator role — implementation of slices 3-9 goes to engineer delegates, not this seat; slices 1-2 were implemented orchestrator-direct and put through full review. Review: claude-sonnet-5-5 (Claude family, independent of GLM author), session f3fe915b-0736-44ad-8faf-6c94decb4f64, prompt/findings/stdout under collab/1793132488348-reviewer-yang-slice2*; P2 (nested-quote constant-form? defect) confirmed, reproduced, fixed, resumed reviewer CONFIRMED: \\\"Ready to commit? Yes\\\"; P3s accepted as documentation + ledger entries (conj/assoc resolution via portable primitives, metadata/duplicate-key gaps, oracle-harness cleanup — cleanups applied).\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md:10:blocker and the Phase 1 sign-off's P2 publication gate. This ruling does\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md:262:  P2 -- the revision history (this document); P3 -- `:reasons`\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md:513:    P2, Phase