s/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:3002:| P2 | §7.1 | header/enrollment checks follow walk/frame validation; retained serves survive retry | `lift-task` order, 7a D4 |\\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.md:23:> There should be no concept of a server or client. its P2P but client/server\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.rust.md:1050:(the P2P invariant of `dao.stream`). Concretely:\\ndocs/design/dao.space.index.as-observer.md:801:| F1 | Phase 0′'s `pr-str`/`read-string` round trip of a live session cannot pass: `BTSet` prints elements-only, a storage handle is unprintable (glm P2) | Phase 0′ round-trips the *checkpoint value* instead and compares `restored-indexes` to the live trees |\\ndocs/design/dao.space.index.as-observer.md:802:| F2 | Draining the recording handle is unsafe on the resumed-checkpoint path on the JVM: `-store-tree!` rewrites the wrapper's restore source and a soft-ref'd root refaults through the drained handle (glm P2) | §4.1 states the invariant (refaults resolve against durable content, never the handle) and pins index-session roots `:strong`; re-restore after flush rejected because materialization is asynchronous; Phase 0′ test |\\ndocs/design/dao.space.index.as-observer.md:811:| N1 | The `:strong` remedy binds to the session's recording storage, but ref-pinning consults the *tree's* settings; a session resumed via `open-published!`/`restored-indexes` gets the JVM `:soft` default and the F2 sequence survives (glm P2) | §4.1 states where settings come from per session kind; a resumed session restores through a session-constructed `:strong` `kv-storage`, never the query read path; §4.2 reworded |\\ndocs/design/dao.space.index.as-observer.md:827:| A4 | \\\"Retain the exact list\\\" is not per-payload progress; the `run-on-stream` progress defect bites an indexer whose round finishes a publication then throws (astra P2) | §4.1 state machine `{:payloads :next}`, advance per `ok`, terminal outcomes throw with `:next` preserved; at-most-once per staged occurrence stated as the guarantee; Phase 0′ gated on the observer fix |\\ndocs/design/dao.space.index.as-observer.md:828:| A5 | The index state is not a `query/value?`; \\\"after each appended batch\\\" is not an observation boundary (astra P2) | §5: `index/db-value` builds an in-process covered value on the `open-published!` shape; \\\"live\\\" defined as every batch folded up to the cursor after a round; Phase 1 test reworded |\\ndocs/design/dao.space.index.as-observer.md:829:| A6 | The mode rule missed positive declared-ref `v` on `:unresolved` media, tempid `v` on `:resolved` media, id zero, and `m` (astra P2) | §3.1 mode matrix over `e`, declared-ref `v`, `m`, with reserved ids |\\ndocs/design/dao.space.index.as-observer.md:830:| A7 | A checkpoint alone cannot yield the writer watermark when retained transactions follow its cursor; the in-process task restart was excluded (astra P2) | §4.2: `:max-t` at capture plus the folded suffix; three restart cases distinguished; \\\"one truth\\\" argued, not assumed |\\ndocs/design/dao.space.index.as-observer.md:831:| A8 | Outer batch grammar unspecified (a record map iterated as a batch would see map entries); rejected batch's state transition unspecified (astra P2) | §2.2 step 0 grammar; atomic-per-batch rule with `:batch` advanced exactly once |\\ndocs/design/dao.space.index.as-observer.md:832:| A9 | Manifest equality is not a valid acceptance test: `from-sequential` and `conj` partition the same rows differently (JVM probe) (astra P2) | Phase 0′ requires logical equality — rows, counts, query results, valid restore — with enough rows to force splits |\\ndocs/design/dao.space.index.as-observer.md:840:| R1 | `publish!`/`checkpoint`/`db-value` over `index-state` alone cannot see `:cursor` or `:ingress-gaps`, which live in the observer half (astra P2) | §2.1: `checkpoint` and `coverage` take the session; `db-value` stays over the consumer; `restore` returns the consumer and the composition re-attaches at `c` (`attach` gains a kept-cursor argument) |\\ndocs/design/dao.space.index.as-observer.md:841:| R2 | Draining `:defects` erases the only record that the index is partial (astra P2) | §2.2: monotonic `:rejected` separate from drainable `:defects`; carried in coverage and checkpoint |\\ndocs/design/dao.space.index.as-observer.md:842:| R3 | \\\"Reserved\\\" overlapped tempids; reserved `e` rejected on `:resolved` contradicts `local-datom?` and breaks parity (astra P2; glm R4-1, R4-4) | §3.1: disjoint tempid/reserved/user-positive partition; reserved `e` passes on `:resolved`, stated as a decision |\\ndocs/design/dao.space.index.as-observer.md:843:| R4 | Empty batches have no greatest `t`; `:max-t` had no empty-history value; within-row order unspecified (astra P2; glm R4-2) | §2.2: empty batch advances the ordinal only; `:max-t` is `nil` until a row folds, watermark `0` then; order `e`, `v`, `m` |\\ndocs/design/dao.space.index.as-observer.md:844:| R5 | Restoring a session-local `:ids` can rewind a shared allocator (astra P2) | §4.2: `restore` refuses `:shared`; coordinated recovery deferred (§8) |\\ndocs/design/yang.typescript.md:126:  prelude pattern (P2, P3, I1 to I6). They do not depend on L-a, L-e, the DHT\\ndocs/design/yang.typescript.md:1698:  surface, the linked-matrix and tick dependencies), five P2s and one P3.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ncollab/orch-lane/1795400000000-architect-b2r3-confirm.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:16:{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_8\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"which -a git clojure php; rg --files collab/orch-lane | rg 'b2r2|roundB2-r3|b2r3|roundB2.*findings'; cat .agents/skills/code-review-pr/references/review_checklist.md; sed -n '1,150p' .agents/skills/code-review-pr/scripts/pr_reviewer.py\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\ncollab/orch-lane/1795400000000-architect-b2r3-confirm.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:17:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_8\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"which -a git clojure php; rg --files collab/orch-lane | rg 'b2r2|roundB2-r3|b2r3|roundB2.*findings'; cat .agents/skills/code-review-pr/references/review_checklist.md; sed -n '1,150p' .agents/skills/code-review-pr/scripts/pr_reviewer.py\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"/usr/bin/git\\n/Users/sto/.local/share/mise/installs/clojure/1.12.4.1602/bin/clojure\\n/opt/homebrew/bin/clojure\\n/opt/homebrew/bin/clojure\\ncollab/orch-lane/1795400000000-architect-b2r3-confirm.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log\\ncollab/orch-lane/1795300000000-engineer-roundB2-r3.muse-spark-1.3-contributor.stdout.log\\ncollab/orch-lane/1795250000000-architect-b2r2-confirm.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log\\n# Code Review PR Checklist & Taxonomy\\n\\nWhen performing code reviews, evaluate changes using this structured checklist and severity taxonomy.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Finding Severity Taxonomy\\n\\n| Severity | Label | Definition | Examples |\\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\\n| **P0** | **Critical (Blocker)** | Security vulnerabilities, data loss risks, production crashes, secret leakage. Must be fixed before merging. | Hardcoded tokens, unhandled NullPointer on critical path, SQL injection, broken auth check. |\\n| **P1** | **High (Must Address)** | Logic bugs, breaking API changes, missing error handling on external calls, race conditions, lack of tests for complex logic. | Swallowed exceptions, broken retry loop, missing backward compatibility in API schema. |\\n| **P2** | **Medium (Recommended)** | Performance inefficiencies, code duplication, sub-optimal data structures, non-idiomatic style. | Unnecessary DB query inside loop, missing index, missing parameter validation. |\\n| **P3** | **Low (Nit / Suggestion)** | Minor formatting, naming improvements, leftover comments/TODOs, minor doc polish. | Variable naming clarity, typos in docstrings, cleaning leftover TODO comments. |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Comprehensive Review Checklist\\n\\n### A. Logic & Correctness\\n- [ ] **Edge Cases**: Does the code handle null/nil/undefined, empty collections, zero values, boundary numbers, and unexpected inputs?\\n- [ ] **State & Concurrency**: Are shared state mutations thread-safe? Are locks acquired/released properly without deadlock risks?\\n- [ ] **Control Flow**: Are all conditional branches covered? Do loops have guaranteed termination conditions?\\n- [ ] **Error Propagation**: Are errors caught and logged/surfaced appropriately, rather than swallowed silently (`catch (Exception e) {}`)?\\n\\n### B. Security & Credentials\\n- [ ] **No Hardcoded Secrets**: Are API keys, passwords, bearer tokens, or private keys excluded from code and config?\\n- [ ] **Input Validation & Sanitization**: Are external inputs validated before processing or passing to system shells, DB queries, or HTML rendering?\\n- [ ] **Authentication & Authorization**: Do endpoints verify user identity and check permissions before executing state changes?\\n- [ ] **Safe Dependencies**: Are newly added packages pinned to trusted versions without known vulnerabilities?\\n\\n### C. Architecture & API Design\\n- [ ] **Preserve API Contracts**: Are public method signatures, REST endpoints, and schema definitions backward compatible?\\n- [ ] **Single Responsibility**: Are modules, classes, and functions focused on a clear, single responsibility?\\n- [ ] **Coupling & Cohesion**: Is the new code properly modularized without introducing circular dependencies or leaky abstractions?\\n- [ ] **Idempotence**: Are retry loops or state-changing operations safe to re-execute on transient failures?\\n\\n### D. Performance & Resource Efficiency\\n- [ ] **N+1 Queries**: Are database or remote API calls executed in batches rather than inside loops?\\n- [ ] **Resource Cleanup**: Are file handles, database connections, streams, and web sockets closed explicitly (or managed via try-with-resources / context managers)?\\n- [ ] **Memory & Allocation**: Are large datasets streamed or paginated rather than loaded fully into memory at once?\\n\\n### E. Test Coverage & Quality\\n- [ ] **Test Coverage**: Do new features or bug fixes include corresponding unit or integration tests?\\n- [ ] **Test Quality**: Do tests verify actual assertions rather than just checking that code runs without throwing?\\n- [ ] **Edge Case Tests**: Are failure modes, invalid inputs, and error handlers covered by unit tests?\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. Review Feedback Guidelines\\n\\n1. **Be Specific**: Always reference the exact file line number, function name, and context.\\n2. **Explain the \\\"Why\\\"**: Don't just say \\\"change this\\\". Explain the risk or benefit (e.g., \\\"This could lead to a race condition if two threads call `transact!` simultaneously...\\\").\\n3. **Provide Concrete Fixes**: Offer concrete, copy-pasteable diff snippets where appropriate.\\n4. **Acknowledge Good Work**: Highlight well-crafted solutions, thorough tests, or clean refactorings.\\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nPR Reviewer Utility Script for Git-based Code Reviews.\\nParses git diffs, analyzes churn and file risk categories, scans for security smells\\nand debugging code, and produces structured markdown or JSON review reports.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nimport argparse\\nimport json\\nimport os\\nimport re\\nimport subprocess\\nimport sys\\nfrom dataclasses import asdict, dataclass, field\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nfrom typing import Dict, List, Optional, Tuple\\n\\n\\n@dataclass\\nclass Finding:\\n    severity: str  # P0 (Critical), P1 (High), P2 (Medium), P3 (Low)\\n    category: str  # Security, Debug, Quality, ErrorHandling, TestCoverage\\n    file_path: str\\n    line_number: Optional[int]\\n    message: str\\n    snippet: str\\n\\n\\n@dataclass\\nclass FileStat:\\n    path: str\\n    additions: int\\n    deletions: int\\n    category: str\\n    risk_level: str  # High, Medium, Low\\n\\n\\n@dataclass\\nclass ReviewSummary:\\n    target: str\\n    total_files: int\\n    total_additions: int\\n    total_deletions: int\\n    test_additions: int\\n    source_additions: int\\n    test_to_source_ratio: float\\n    file_stats: List[FileStat] = field(default_factory=list)\\n    findings: List[Finding] = field(default_factory=list)\\n    commits: List[str] = field(default_factory=list)\\n\\n\\ndef run_git_command(args: List[str], cwd: Optional[str] = None) -> str:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Helper to run git commands cleanly.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    cmd = [\\\"git\\\"] + args\\n    try:\\n        res = subprocess.run(\\n            cmd,\\n            cwd=cwd,\\n            stdout=subprocess.PIPE,\\n            stderr=subprocess.PIPE,\\n            text=True,\\n            check=True,\\n        )\\n        return res.stdout.strip()\\n    except subprocess.CalledProcessError as e:\\n        sys.stderr.write(f\\\"Git command failed: {' '.join(cmd)}\\\\nError: {e.stderr}\\\\n\\\")\\n        raise RuntimeError(f\\\"Git execution failed: {e.stderr.strip()}\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef categorize_file(file_path: str) -> Tuple[str, str]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Categorizes file type and assigns risk level.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    path_lower = file_path.lower()\\n\\n    # Security & Auth\\n    if any(k in path_lower for k in [\\\"auth\\\", \\\"secret\\\", \\\"crypto\\\", \\\"token\\\", \\\"permission\\\", \\\"jwt\\\", \\\"oauth\\\", \\\"password\\\"]):\\n        return \\\"Security/Auth\\\", \\\"High\\\"\\n\\n    # Database & Schema\\n    if any(k in path_lower for k in [\\\"migration\\\", \\\"schema\\\", \\\".sql\\\", \\\"entity\\\", \\\"db/\\\"]):\\n        return \\\"Database/Schema\\\", \\\"High\\\"\\n\\n    # Infrastructure & Config\\n    if any(k in path_lower for k in [\\\"docker\\\", \\\"terraform\\\", \\\".tf\\\", \\\".env\\\", \\\"k8s\\\", \\\"helm\\\", \\\"ci/cd\\\", \\\".github/workflows\\\"]):\\n        return \\\"Infra/Config\\\", \\\"High\\\"\\n    if any(file_path.endswith(ext) for ext in [\\\"package.json\\\", \\\"deps.edn\\\", \\\"Cargo.toml\\\", \\\"go.mod\\\", \\\"requirements.txt\\\", \\\"pom.xml\\\", \\\"build.gradle\\\"]):\\n        return \\\"Dependencies\\\", \\\"Medium\\\"\\n\\n    # API / Interfaces\\n    if any(k in path_lower for k in [\\\"proto\\\", \\\"openapi\\\", \\\"swagger\\\", \\\"graphql\\\", \\\"router\\\", \\\"controller\\\", \\\"api/\\\"]):\\n        return \\\"API/Contract\\\", \\\"Medium\\\"\\n\\n    # Tests\\n    if any(k in path_lower for k in [\\\"test\\\", \\\"spec\\\", \\\"mock\\\", \\\"fixture\\\", \\\"e2e\\\"]):\\n        return \\\"Tests\\\", \\\"Low\\\"\\n\\n    # Documentation\\n    if any(file_path.endswith(ext) for ext in [\\\".md\\\", \\\".rst\\\", \\\".txt\\\", \\\"LICENSE\\\"]):\\n        return \\\"Documentation\\\", \\\"Low\\\"\\n\\n    # Core source\\n    return \\\"Source Code\\\", \\\"Medium\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef scan_diff_content(diff_text: str) -> List[Finding]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Scans diff text for added code smells and risks.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    findings: List[Finding] = []\\n\\n    # Patterns to match added lines\\n    patterns = [\\n        # Secret leaks\\n        (\\n            r\\\"(?i)^\\\\+.*(api[_\\\\-]?key|secret[_\\\\-]?key|bearer\\\\s+[a-z0-9_\\\\-\\\\.]{20,}|private[_\\\\-]?key)\\\\s*[:=]\\\\s*['\\\\\\\"][A-Za-z0-9%+\\\\/=\\\\-_]{8,}['\\\\\\\"]\\\",\\n            \\\"P0\\\",\\n            \\\"Security\\\",\\n            \\\"Possible hardcoded credential or secret detected.\\\",\\n        ),\\n        (\\n            r\\\"^\\\\+.*-----BEGIN (RSA|OPENSSH|EC|PRIVATE) KEY-----\\\",\\n            \\\"P0\\\",\\n            \\\"Security\\\",\\n            \\\"Embedded private key detected.\\\",\\n        ),\\n        # Debug code left behind\\n        (\\n            r\\\"^\\\\+.*\\\\b(console\\\\.log|print\\\\(|debugger;|binding\\\\.pry|import pdb; pdb\\\\.set_trace|println!|fmt\\\\.Println)\\\\b\\\",\\n            \\\"P3\\\",\\n            \\\"Debug\\\",\\n            \\\"Leftover debug statement detected.\\\",\\n        ),\\n        # Dangerous functions\\n        (\\n            r\\\"^\\\\+.*\\\\b(eval\\\\(|exec\\\\(|os\\\\.system\\\\(|subprocess\\\\.Popen\\\\(.*shell\\\\s*=\\\\s*True|dangerouslySetInnerHTML)\\\\b\\\",\\n            \\\"P1\\\",\\n            \\\"Security\\\",\\n            \\\"Potentially unsafe dynamic execution or shell invocation.\\\",\\n        ),\\n        # Swallowed exceptions\\n        (\\n            r\\\"^\\\\+.*\\\\b(catch\\\\s*\\\\([^\\\\)]*\\\\)\\\\s*\\\\{\\\\s*\\\\}|except:\\\\s*pass|rescue\\\\s*=>\\\\s*nil)\\\\b\\\",\\n            \\\"P2\\\",\\n            \\\"ErrorHandling\\\",\\n            \\\"Swallowed exception without logging or handling.\\\",\\n        ),\\n        # Potential SQL Injection\\n        (\\n            r\\\"(?i)^\\\\+.*((select|insert|update|delete)\\\\s+.*%s|(select|insert|update|delete)\\\\s+.*\\\\$[a-z0-9_]+|(select|insert|update|delete)\\\\s+.*\\\\+\\\\s*[a-z0-9_]+)\\\",\\n            \\\"P1\\\",\\n            \\\"Security\\\",\\n            \\\"Potential SQL string concatenation detected. Use parameterized queries.\\\",\\n        ),\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ncollab/orch-lane/1795400000000-architect-b2r3-confirm.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:18:{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_9\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"rg -n 'B2-r2|B2-r3|landing|destruct|P2|stream' collab/orch-lane/1795250000000* collab/orch-lane/1795300000000* collab/orch-lane/1795400000000* | tail -60\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\ncollab/orch-lane/1795250000000-architect-b2r2-confirm.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:3:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_0\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"I’ll check the pushed tip against the step-7 findings, trace the stream wiring, and verify the available gate evidence.\"}}\ncollab/orch-lane/1795250000000-architect-b2r2-confirm.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:5:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_1\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -