gs (muse-spark-1.3-contributor)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nTask: `/tmp/muse-p8-fixes2.md` (the three residuals from the landing-review r2).\\\\\\\\nBranch: `feat/p8-legacy-retirement`. No push (laptop-legal).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## 1. Provenance (`:measured-at`)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n`test/yang/php/antlr/phpt_quick_mismatch_manifest.edn`: the five\\\\\\\\n`gc_013` / `gc_023` / `bug39438` / `bug64660` / `gc_012` records cited\\\\\\\\n`{:tree \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"06cd429f\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" :date \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"2026-11-04\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}`, but `06cd429f` committed\\\\\\\\n2026-11-06 02:31 +0700 — the tree did not exist on the cited date, so the\\\\\\\\npair is impossible. The engine-results were recorded from the Nov-4 oracle\\\\\\\\npass (manifest regenerated in `2e5f7f2f`, 2026-11-04 12:36 +0700); the exact\\\\\\\\nshiva checkout hash of that run was never recorded, so per the task brief no\\\\\\\\nhash was invented: all five now carry `:tree \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"unrecorded\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"`, keeping the\\\\\\\\nsupported `:date \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"2026-11-04\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"`, `:host \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"shiva\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"`, and `:log\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"~/ci/rm-phpt-quick.log\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"`. `bug40809` keeps `{:tree \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"dbe9e072\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" :date\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"2026-11-05\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" :log \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"~/ci/rm-40809-long.log\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}` (the 90-min remeasure; already\\\\\\\\ncorrect). No code reads `:measured-at` (EDN data only); re-validated 6 gaps,\\\\\\\\n6 measured via `clojure.edn`.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## 2. JSON depth off-by-one (`prelude_p9.cljc`, `php/json-encode`)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe container guard was `(>= (+ depth 1) maxdepth)`, failing `[1]` at depth\\\\\\\\n1. Now `(> (+ depth 1) maxdepth)`: `json_encode([1],0,1)` → `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"[1]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"`,\\\\\\\\n`json_encode([[1]],0,1)` → `false`. Test pins updated in\\\\\\\\n`builtin_surfaces_test.clj`: the `[1],0,1` var_dump pin is now `string(3)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"[1]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"` (diag still `[]`), plus a new `[[1]],0,1` → `bool(false)` pin. The\\\\\\\\nnew pins failed before the fix (3 failures incl. the two scanner pins) and\\\\\\\\npass after.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## 3. JSON number scanner (`prelude_p9.cljc`, `php/json-number`)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n`php/num-prefix` (PHP juggling; untouched) accepts `.1` and `1.` as full\\\\\\\\nnumbers, but the JSON grammar needs digits on both sides of the point. Added\\\\\\\\n`php/json-dot-bad-at` / `php/json-dot-bad?`: any `.` in the token without a\\\\\\\\ndigit on both sides is a syntax error. `1e+2` stays valid (no point in the\\\\\\\\ntoken); `1e+` truncation and leading-plus/leading-zero rejection unchanged.\\\\\\\\nNew pins: `json_decode('.1')` and `json_decode('1.')` → `NULL`.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Gate\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- `clojure -M:test -n yang.php.antlr.builtin-surfaces-test -n\\\\\\\\n  yang.php.antlr.request-context-test`: 6 tests, 205 assertions, 0 failures,\\\\\\\\n  0 errors.\\\\\\\\n- `clojure -M:kondo --lint` on both touched code files: 0 errors, 0 warnings.\\\\\\\\n- cljstyle: attempted 2026-11-06 on this laptop via the only local artifact\\\\\\\\n  (`mvxcvi/cljstyle 0.16.626` jar in `~/.m2`; `CLJ_OFFLINE=true clojure\\\\\\\\n  -Sdeps ... -M -m cljstyle.main check` on both touched files). It fails\\\\\\\\n  before linting: `cljstyle.config/read-file` gets `nil` from\\\\\\\\n  `(io/resource \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"cljstyle/indents.clj\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")` — the cached jar contains only\\\\\\\\n  `config.clj`, `main.clj`, `task/`, `format/` and ships no `indents.clj`\\\\\\\\n  resource (verified by unzipping it), and Maven is unreachable offline to\\\\\\\\n  re-fetch. No other runnable cljstyle exists on the laptop (no binary on\\\\\\\\n  `PATH`, none vendored; prior seats used `0.17.642`, absent from the\\\\\\\\n  cache). Gate therefore unrun; the edits reuse the exact neighboring\\\\\\\\n  indentation/comment conventions, and kondo is clean.\\\\\\\\n4:    [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\\\\\\\\n9: