\\\\\"str_replace\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" args 3 4 \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"at least 3\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")\\\\\\\\n1794860000000-architect-confirm4.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log     test(yang.php): the bug44069 slow-gap record removed — str_repeat passes on the merged tree (measured on shiva)\\\\\\\\n1794860000000-architect-confirm4.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log commit dbe9e072c45b6c9ef198da0123c23d49e3b79558\\\\\\\\n1794860000000-architect-confirm4.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log     49\\\\\\\\t   :engine-result {:timeout \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\">5400 s with str_repeat present (the stress loop executes for real; measured on shiva 2026-11-04, 90-min window)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"},\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}}\\\\ncollab/orch-lane/1795060000000-architect-p8-final-confirm3.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:49:{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_24\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"/Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/usr/bin/python3 -c 'import json,pathlib\\\\\\\\nfor prefix in [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"179482\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"179486\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"179490\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]:\\\\\\\\n for p in pathlib.Path(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"collab/orch-lane\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\").glob(prefix+\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"*.stdout.log\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"):\\\\\\\\n  for line in p.open():\\\\\\\\n   try: obj=json.loads(line)\\\\\\\\n   except ValueError: continue\\\\\\\\n   item=obj.get(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",{})\\\\\\\\n   if item.get(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")==\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"agent_message\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" and (\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"procedure\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" in item.get(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\") or \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"P8 —\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" in item.get(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")): print(p.name, item[\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"])\\\\\\\\n   out=item.get(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")\\\\\\\\n   if \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"For \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'`bug44069`, `bug40809`, and `bug63055`:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" in out and len(out)<20000: print(out)'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"' \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"1794720000000-architect-confirm-round.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log\\\\\\\\nI’ll check the architecture rules and both commits, then give each unit a verdict. For P8, I’ll distinguish approval of the procedure from confirmation of the pending measured records.\\\\\\\\nI’m using the code-review-pr skill for this confirmation pass, focused on the cited fixes and their acceptance boundaries.\\\\\\\\nThe P1 diff removes the out-of-scope `fesc` reference and places the drain after the shutdown escape. The P8 manifest still has the three stale records, consistent with the remeasurement being pending. I’m checking the P9 edge cases and P1 fatal-bypass path before assigning verdicts.\\\\\\\\nP9 still has contract defects despite the reported green gate: diff/intersect use loose equality, negative `strrpos` offsets remain wrong, and JSON encoding does not propagate nested failure correctly. The new tests also assert a nonexistent extraction constant. I’m checking the counterexamples against PHP 8.3 source so the required follow-up is concrete.\\\\\\\\nFocused JVM probes reproduced the P9 failures: nested `json_encode([INF])` raises a host error, `json_decode(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"+1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")` returns `1`, and encoding ignores the supplied depth. For P1, the bundled closure check and linked-module manifest construction pass, and the shutdown-exit case returns `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"AS\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"` with status `3`.\\\\\\\\n**1. `d5f120d0` — CONFIRMED.**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe follow-up resolves both findings, including the linked-module boundary.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- Bundled free-name checking returns no stray names; `module-spec` constructs successfully.\\\\\\\\n- The shutdown-exit probe returns **`\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"AS\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"`, status `3`**.\\\\\\\\n- Injecting `php/root-fatal` during the buffered shutdown callback returns **empty output and fatal `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"boom\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"`**, bypassing the drain.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe seat may land this unit. [Corrected fallback and drain placement](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p1fix/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:5189).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**2. `0aa234e9` — DEFECT. Hold landing.**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nEmpty-search handling, nontruncating padding, single-array mapping keys, variadic mapping, null-binding existence, missing-name compact warnings, and the declaration-based resolution guard are repaired. Residual defects remain:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- **P1 — Nested JSON encoding failure escapes into a host error.** `json_encode([INF])` reproduces `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"data primitive refused\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"`: the array encoder concatenates its opening delimiter with the child’s `false` result. Without throw mode, PHP returns `false` without the newly introduced warning. [Encoder](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b1/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude_p9.cljc:648), [PHP 8.3 implementation](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/php/php-src/PHP-8.3/ext/json/json.c).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- **P2 — Negative `strrpos` offsets remain incorrect.** `strrpos(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"hello\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"l\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", -2)` reproduces **2**; PHP requires **3**. The new test pins the wrong answer. Offsets outside the haystack also need `ValueError`. [Implementation](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b1/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude_p9.cljc:52), [incorrect assertion](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b1/test/yang/php/antlr/builtin_surfaces_test.clj:37), [PHP source](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/php/php-src/PHP-8.3/ext/standard/string.c).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- **P2 — Array comparisons remain wrong.** Diff/intersect still use loose equality: `count(array_diff([\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"1.0\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"], [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]))` reproduces **0**, requiring **1** under [PHP’s string comparison](https://www.php.net/manual/en/function.array-diff.php). Unique’s flag dispatch is also misnumbered: `SORT_REGULAR` is **0**, numeric **1**, string **2**. The regular-mode counterexample reproduces two retained values instead of one. [Comparison code](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b1/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude_p9.cljc:503), [PHP flag definitions](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/php/php-src/PHP-8.3/ext/standard/php_array.h).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- **P2 — Splice replacement conversion is incomplete.** Reusing `spread-loop` preserves replacement string keys, which PHP discards. Explicit `null` becomes one null element instead of an empty replacement array. [Splice implementation](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b1/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude_p9.cljc:431), [PHP contract](https://www.php.net/manual/en/function.array-splice.php).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- **P2 — JSON grammar, depth, and options remain incomplete.** `json_decode(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"+1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")` reproduces integer **1**; raw control characters are also accepted. Encoding ignores argument 3: `json_encode([[1]], 0, 1)` succeeds. Decoding depth starts one level too low: `[1]` at depth 1 succeeds instead of failing. Other unsupported flags remain silently accepted. [Number parser](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b1/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude_p9.cljc:761), [depth/options](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b1/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude_p9.cljc:695), [PHP scanner](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/php/php-src/PHP-8.3/ext/json/json_scanner.re), [PHP depth initialization](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/php/php-src/PHP-8.3/ext/json/json_parser.y).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- **P2 — Extract/compact completion is overstated.** `EXTR_PREFIX_ONLY_IF_EXISTS` remains a nonexistent constant, now asserted by the tests. Invalid extraction modes, missing required prefixes, and invalid prefixes lack required validation. `EXTR_PREFIX_ALL` incorrectly rejects numeric keys: the focused probe imports **0** variables for `[0 => 5]` with prefix `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"p\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"`; PHP imports `$p_0`. Empty prefixes also lose the mandatory underscore. `compact(1)` silently skips its required warning. [Constants](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b1/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/builtins.cljc:169), [extract/compact](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b1/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude_module.cljc:200), [PHP extraction and compact implementation](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/php/php-src/PHP-8.3/ext/standard/array.c).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe reported **3/135/0** gate therefore does not establish contract completion. Correct the erroneous assertions and cover these counterexamples.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**3. P8 manifest — CONFIRMED-WITH-EDITS, pending measured fold.**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**The remeasure-and-fold procedure satisfies my ruling.** No additional semantic requirement is imposed.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nFor `bug44069`, `bug40809`, and `bug63055`:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- Remove records that now pass.\\\\\\\\n- For remaining failures, fold the measured result and update the classification/work item.\\\\\\\\n- Retain the measured tree identity and run evidence; distinguish resource failures or timeouts from guest results.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nI independently checked **95 unique quick IDs**, matching descriptions and recorded total. The three stale slow records remain in the inspected artifact. The seat may land after folding the measurements and checking manifest consistency; this is conditional authority, not confirmation of results still pending.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nRead-only review completed with focused JVM probes and static/source checks. No files changed or suites rerun.\\\\\\\\n1794680000000-architect-consolidated-round.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log\\\\\\\\nI’ll read the architecture rules and the four worktree diffs, then issue the three verdicts with file-and-line evidence and landing authority. I’ll keep this pass read-only and leave behavioral validation to the recorded shiva gates.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nI’m applying the repository’s `code-review-pr` skill, using your requested verdict format and static-only scope.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nTwo concrete issues have surfaced: the P5 fold commit has malformed fixture calls that the laptop working tree repairs, and the P1 shutdown fallback references `fesc` outside its lexical binding. I’m tracing whether that shutdown branch is reachable and checking the terminal escape and include boundaries before deciding landing authority.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe terminal escape bypasses guest handlers and finalizers as intended. The out-of-scope `fesc` also creates a free name in the linked PHP module, so the bundled safepoint tests do not establish that includes still work. The P5 diagnostics need separate rulings: missing diagnostics are engine behavior; location text and errno classification are different comparison concerns.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nP8’s quick manifest is internally consistent: 95 unique mismatch IDs, matching descriptions and family counts, plus eight slow-gap records. But three slow records still expect undefined `str_repeat` or `str_replace` after the merged P9 tree registers both builtins. Those records need fresh measurements on the merged tree. The cell-reference change looks sound, including the shared callable fallback.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe landing decision is now clear: the cell-reference branch can land; P1, P8, and P5 need forward fixes. One additional P1 edge remains: `exit()` inside a shutdown callback escapes past the new buffer drain, so an open buffer can still lose output. I’m consolidating the exact fixes and the three diagnostic rulings.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**Verdict 1 — DEFECT: `0eade311` needs another forward fix.**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- **Exhaustion escape: CONFIRMED.** `php/abandon-to` only pops frames; it executes no guest finalizers. The captured continuation then bypasses guest handlers and returns. [prelude.cljc:214](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p1fix/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:214)\\\\\\\\n- **Shutdown termination: CONFIRMED-WITH-EDITS.** Safepoint exhaustion reaches the stored fatal continuation during shutdown. However, the operational-`exc2` fallback calls **out-of-scope `fesc`**. Replace that call with `(php/root-fatal (get exc2 :message))`. [prelude.cljc:5189](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p1fix/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:5189)\\\\\\\\n- **Budget domain: CONFIRMED.** The constructor rejects negative integers, fractional values, strings, and other nonintegers with named host-side `:invalid-budget`. Zero is admitted. [safepoint.cljc:43](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p1fix/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/safepoint.cljc:43)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**The include-unit boundary regresses even with unlimited execution.** The stray `fesc` becomes a free name in the PHP runtime module; module publication rejects undeclared names before execution. This is independent of whether the fallback executes. [prelude.cljc:5505](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p1fix/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:5505), [core/prelude.cljc:152](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p1fix/src/cljc/yang/core/prelude.cljc:152). The bundled harness still leaves the AST uninstrumented when no budget is supplied. [e2e_harness.clj:97](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p1fix/test/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj:97)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe additional Round-A repairs are partly confirmed: ordinary `exit` now skips guest `finally` and preserves status; normal shutdown drains nested buffers. **Buffer draining remains defective when a shutdown callback exits.** For example, `ob_start(); register_shutdown_function(function(){ echo 'S'; exit(3); }); echo 'A';` escapes past the drain and renders buffer zero, losing buffered output. Move mandatory buffer draining outside the shutdown escape, while retaining the operational-fatal bypass. [prelude.cljc:485](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p1fix/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:485), [prelude.cljc:3942](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p1fix/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:3942), [prelude.cljc:5195](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p1fix/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:5195)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**Verdict 2 — CONFIRMED-WITH-EDITS: the three design rulings.**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- **(a) Empty `ob_end_clean`: engine implementation gap.** Preserve the recorded notice. Change the no-buffer arm to emit `php/warn` with errno **8** and the recorded message, then return `false`. Do not normalize away a missing diagnostic: handlers and reporting masks can observe it. [prelude.cljc:390](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p5r/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:390)\\\\\\\\n- **(b) Headers-already-sent text: permit narrow comparison normalization.** Strip only the location suffix ` by (output started at …:line)` from the oracle message. Preserve the warning, errno, and message prefix; retain the full raw observation. The engine’s deliberate shorter form may remain. [prelude.cljc:404](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p5r/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:404), [programs_p5.cljc:52](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p5r/test/yang/php/antlr/programs_p5.cljc:52)\\\\\\\\n- **(c) 1024 versus 8: runner classification artifact; engine stays 1024.** `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Notice\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"→8` cannot identify `E_USER_NOTICE`. Preserve the old observation as explicitly class-derived; keep the engine semantic expectation at **1024**. Until exact errno recording replaces it, permit **1024→8 only in comparison against marked class-derived observations**, not as a global diagnostic rewrite. [oracle.clj:36](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p5r/src/dev/yang/php/oracle.clj:36), [oracle.clj:98](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p5r/src/dev/yang/php/oracle.clj:98)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**Verdict 3(a) — DEFECT: P8 at `bab43c51`.**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe legacy compiler deletion and executable-reference sweep are complete. The REPL and demo use the ANTLR route, and subsystem routing is retargeted. The migrated corpus uses PHP expectations with an honest hand-derived banner. [frontends.cljc:83](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p8/src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc:83), [subsystems.edn:62](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p8/src/dev/subsystems.edn:62), [programs_p8.cljc:6](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p8/test/yang/php/antlr/programs_p8.cljc:6)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe quick manifest is internally consistent: **95 unique IDs**, matching description keys; families **10 GC / 16 foreach-by-reference / 3 unset / 3 named / 63 other**; recorded unsupported count **57**. All eight slow records match their selection entries’ expectation fields. [manifest.edn:90](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p8/test/yang/php/antlr/phpt_quick_mismatch_manifest.edn:90)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**Blocking defect:** slow records `bug44069`, `bug40809`, and `bug63055` still expect undefined `str_repeat`/`str_replace`, although the merged tree registers and implements both. Remeasure those three on the merged tree; remove records that now pass or record their actual remaining failure. Do not infer replacement outcomes from static reading. [manifest.edn:45](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p8/test/yang/php/antlr/phpt_quick_mismatch_manifest.edn:45), [manifest.edn:79](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p8/test/yang/php/antlr/phpt_quick_mismatch_manifest.edn:79), [builtins.cljc:56](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p8/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/builtins.cljc:56)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**Verdict 3(b) — DEFECT: P5 fold at `3a2ce4da`.**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nRequired edits:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- **Commit the existing laptop fixture repair.** The committed fold puts metadata before the positional output argument and closes calls prematurely; the working-tree diff repairs those malformed forms. The repaired file is still uncommitted. [programs_p5.cljc:37](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p5r/test/yang/php/antlr/programs_p5.cljc:37)\\\\\\\\n- Apply Verdict 2 consistently to oracle and engine comparisons. The current engine gate compares diagnostics literally, so the repaired fixtures still disagree on the three ruled cases. [request_context_test.clj:23](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p5r/test/yang/php/antlr/request_context_test.clj:23)\\\\\\\\n- Fix `request-pairs` to accept ordered entry vectors. The engine accepts them; the runner silently turns them into empty arrays. For the current typed-array fixture, insertion order, server-field replacement, and GET-then-POST merge construction agree. [oracle.clj:227](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p5r/src/dev/yang/php/oracle.clj:227), [prelude.cljc:335](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p5r/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:335)\\\\\\\\n- Compare fixture `:status` against process `:exit`; currently the runner discards it, leaving the exit-status pins unverified. [oracle.clj:292](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p5r/src/dev/yang/php/oracle.clj:292)\\\\\\\\n- Attach P5 run provenance. The fold printer inherits P3-b’s banner rather than establishing the P5 run’s version/host/date. [oracle.clj:31](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p5r/src/dev/yang/php/oracle.clj:31), [oracle.clj:324](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p5r/src/dev/yang/php/oracle.clj:324)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**Verdict 3(c) — CONFIRMED: cellref sweep at `1636e3e9`.**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nAuthentication precedes shape-based dereferencing. Inauthentic shapes reach ordinary descriptor handling, whose shared implementation also authenticates before dereferencing. Genuine object/function/symbol routing is preserved. The regression pairs cover `typeof`/`kind-of` and receiver propagation with shaped data versus genuine references. [prelude.cljc:135](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cs/src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude.cljc:135), [call.cljc:28](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cs/src/cljc/yang/core/call.cljc:28), [prelude_test.cljc:689](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cs/test/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude_test.cljc:689)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**Landing authority:** `feat/cellref-sweep` may merge now. Hold `feat/p1-forward-fixes`, `feat/p8-legacy-retirement`, and `feat/p5-oracle-recording` for the fixes above and the seat’s corresponding gates. Static review only; no behavioral suites run and no files changed.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1794820000000-architect-confirm3.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log 1. **P1 — CONFIRMED for `d5f120d0`; origin-tip DEFECT.** The commit matches the previously confirmed escape/drain repair. **The seat may land `d5f120d0`.** However, live origin still points to `0eade311`, which lacks that repair. Advance origin before merging.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2. **P5 — DEFECT.** Fixture repair, class-derived errno comparison, ordered request vectors, exit-status checking, and P5 banner are confirmed in `a7cf7a0f`. But `request_context_test.clj:36` removes the empty-`ob_end_clean` notice. Verdict 2 explicitly required emitting errno **8** in the engine and prohibited normalizing away this missing diagnostic. The reported **3/35/0** therefore does not close that finding. Also, live origin remains at `e39e1912`, without `a7cf7a0f`.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n3. **P8 — DEFECT at actual origin tip `dbe9e072`** (`514fae8d` plus timeout fold). Manifest parsing and **95 unique quick IDs / 7 slow records** check out. Residuals:\\\\\\\\n   - `bug40809` still carries `:feature :undefined-builtin` despite its timeout result.\\\\\\\\n   - This tree already registers `str_replace`, defines `php/bi-str-replace`, and includes those definitions in the prelude. The retained undefined-function observation needs reconciliation with that tree.\\\\\\\\n   - The fold supplies no measured-tree hash or run-evidence reference establishing the claimed measurements. Retain those before confirmation; no replacement outcome should be inferred statically.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nRead-only review; no files changed or behavioral suites rerun. Only the exact P1 commit has renewed landing authority.\\\\\\\\nLOG 1794720000000-architect-confirm-round.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log\\\\\\\\nI’ll check the architecture rules and both commits, then give each unit a verdict. For P8, I’ll distinguish approval of the procedure from confirmation of the pending measured records.\\\\\\\\nI’m using the code-review-pr skill for this confirmation pass, focused on the cited fixes and their acceptance boundaries.\\\\\\\\nThe P1 diff removes the out-of-scope `fesc` reference and places the drain after the shutdown escape. The P8 manifest still has the three stale records, consistent with the remeasurement being pending. I’m checking the P9 edge cases and P1 fatal-bypass path before assigning verdicts.\\\\\\\\nP9 still has contract defects despite the reported green gate: diff/intersect use loose equality, negative `strrpos` offsets remain wrong, and JSON encoding does not propagate nested failure correctly. The new tests also assert a nonexistent extraction constant. I’m checking the counterexamples against PHP 8.3 source so the required follow-up is concrete.\\\\\\\\nFocused JVM probes reproduced the P9 failures: nested `json_encode([INF])` raises a host error, `json_decode(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"+1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")` returns `1`, and encoding ignores the supplied depth. For P1, the bundled closure check and linked-module manifest construction pass, and the shutdown-exit case returns `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"AS\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"` with status `3`.\\\\\\\\n**1. `d5f120d0` — CONFIRMED.**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe follow-up resolves both findings, including the linked-module boundary.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- Bundled free-name checking returns no stray names; `module-spec` constructs successfully.\\\\\\\\n- The shutdown-exit probe returns **`\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"AS\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"`, status `3`**.\\\\\\\\n- Injecting `php/root-fatal` during the buffered shutdown callback returns **empty output and fatal `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"boom\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"`**, bypassing the drain.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe seat may land this unit. [Corrected fallback and drain placement](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p1fix/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:5189).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**2. `0aa234e9` — DEFECT. Hold landing.**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nEmpty-search handling, nontruncating padding, single-array mapping keys, variadic mapping, null-binding existence, missing-name compact warnings, and the declaration-based resolution guard are repaired. Residual defects remain:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- **P1 — Nested JSON encoding failure escapes into a host error.** `json_encode([INF])` reproduces `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"data primitive refused\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"`: the array encoder concatenates its opening delimiter with the child’s `false` result. Without throw mode, PHP returns `false` without the newly introduced warning. [Encoder](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b1/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude_p9.cljc:648), [PHP 8.3 implementation](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/php/php-src/PHP-8.3/ext/json/json.c).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- **P2 — Negative `strrpos` offsets remain incorrect.** `strrpos(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"hello\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"l\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", -2)` reproduces **2**; PHP requires **3**. The new test pins the wrong answer. Offsets outside the haystack also need `ValueError`. [Implementation](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b1/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude_p9.cljc:52), [incorrect assertion](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b1/test/yang/php/antlr/builtin_surfaces_test.clj:37), [PHP source](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/php/php-src/PHP-8.3/ext/standard/string.c).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- **P2 — Array comparisons remain wrong.** Diff/intersect still use loose equality: `count(array_diff([\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"1.0\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"], [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]))` reproduces **0**, requiring **1** under [PHP’s string comparison](https://www.php.net/manual/en/function.array-diff.php). Unique’s flag dispatch is also misnumbered: `SORT_REGULAR` is **0**, numeric **1**, string **2**. The regular-mode counterexample reproduces two retained values instead of one. [Comparison code](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b1/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude_p9.cljc:503), [PHP flag definitions](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/php/php-src/PHP-8.3/ext/standard/php_array.h).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- **P2 — Splice replacement conversion is incomplete.** Reusing `spread-loop` preserves replacement string keys, which PHP discards. Explicit `null` becomes one null element instead of an empty replacement array. [Splice implementation](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b1/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude_p9.cljc:431), [PHP contract](https://www.php.net/manual/en/function.array-splice.php).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- **P2 — JSON grammar, depth, and options remain incomplete.** `json_decode(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"+1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")` reproduces integer **1**; raw control characters are also accepted. Encoding ignores argument 3: `json_encode([[1]], 0, 1)` succeeds. Decoding depth starts one level too low: `[1]` at depth 1 succeeds instead of failing. Other unsupported flags remain silently accepted. [Number parser](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b1/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude_p9.cljc:761), [depth/options](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b1/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude_p9.cljc:695), [PHP scanner](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/php/php-src/PHP-8.3/ext/json/json_scanner.re), [PHP depth initialization](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/php/php-src/PHP-8.3/ext/json/json_parser.y).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- **P2 — Extract/compact completion is overstated.** `EXTR_PREFIX_ONLY_IF_EXISTS` remains a nonexistent constant, now asserted by the tests. Invalid extraction modes, missing required prefixes, and invalid prefixes lack required validation. `EXTR_PREFIX_ALL` incorrectly rejects numeric keys: the focused probe imports **0** variables for `[0 => 5]` with prefix `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"p\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"`; PHP imports `$p_0`. Empty prefixes also lose the mandatory underscore. `compact(1)` silently skips its required warning. [Constants](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b1/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/builtins.cljc:169), [extract/compact](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b1/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude_module.cljc:200), [PHP extraction and compact implementation](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/php/php-src/PHP-8.3/ext/standard/array.c).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe reported **3/135/0** gate therefore does not establish contract completion. Correct the erroneous assertions and cover these counterexamples.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**3. P8 manifest — CONFIRMED-WITH-EDITS, pending measured fold.**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**The remeasure-and-fold procedure satisfies my ruling.** No additional semantic requirement is imposed.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nFor `bug44069`, `bug40809`, and `bug63055`:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- Remove records that now pass.\\\\\\\\n- For remaining failures, fold the measured result and update the classification/work item.\\\\\\\\n- Retain the measured tree identity and run evidence; distinguish resource failures or timeouts from guest results.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nI independently checked **95 unique quick IDs**, matching descriptions and recorded total. The three stale slow records remain in the inspected artifact. The seat may land after folding the measurements and checking manifest consistency; this is conditional authority, not confirmation of results still pending.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nRead-only review completed with focused JVM probes and static/source checks. No files changed or suites rerun.\\\\\\\\nLOG 1794820000000-architect-confirm3.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log\\\\\\\\nI’ll use the code-revi