{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b2/.git; cat /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b2/collab/orch-lane/1795300000000-engineer-roundB2-r3.muse-spark-1.3-contributor.findings.md; rg -n 'landing|Step-7|B2|gate' docs/design/yang.php* | tail -45\"","aggregated_output":"gitdir: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.git/worktrees/datomworld-b2\nCreated-Local: 2026-11-08 0x:xx +0700\nCoding-Agent: muse (muse-spark-1.3-contributor, laptop)\nWorktree: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b2 (branch feat/p5b2-lifecycle)\n\n# Task: Round B2-r3 — the residual defects from the architect's r2 confirm\n\nThe architect's r2 confirm log\n(collab/orch-lane/1795250000000-architect-b2r2-confirm...stdout.log) is\nabsent from this checkout, so each item below is implemented from the\ntask text in /tmp/muse-b2r3.md plus the cited file:line anchors and the\nPHP 8.3 sources (php/php-src@php-8.3.35, verified by fetch: head.c for\nsetcookie, Zend/zend_API.c for the count-error wording, main.c behavior\nfor the fatal). The r2 findings files in the lane\n(1795070000000-engineer-roundB2-r2,\n1795150000000-engineer-roundB2) supplied the history.\n\n## Per-item changes\n\n### 1. Guest-fatal destructor suppression (prelude.cljc guest-fatal, run-main)\n\n- `php/guest-fatal` now sets `php.rt/exit-status` to 255 and calls\n  `php/freeze-finalizable` over the finalizable list BEFORE escaping\n  through the exit/shutdown continuation. Marking every existing object\n  destructed first means the ordinary shutdown that still runs (shutdown\n  functions, global/static release, buffer drain) destroys without\n  running destructors — `php/destroy-obj` and `php/shutdown-finalizable`\n  both skip destructed objects — while shutdown-function and buffer\n  output still flow. Probe shape: buffer + shutdown echo, destructor\n  silent (\"BS\", never \"BSD\").\n  [prelude.cljc](src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc)\n- `php/run-main` pins the fatal status 255 when the run ends guest-fatal\n  through the shutdown continuation (which never passed the\n  exit-status cell): `st` falls back to 255 whenever the body or the\n  shutdown terminal is `:guest-fatal`. The body-fatal path already\n  carries 255 via the cell; `php/handle-uncaught` with a null exception\n  is identity, so skipping it on the now-non-null status changes\n  nothing.\n  [prelude.cljc](src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc)\n- Fixtures: all four guest-fatal fixtures now pin `:status 255`, plus a\n  new `:trigger-user-error-suppresses-destructors` fixture (live object\n  with `__destruct`, shutdown function, plain echo: out `BS`, fatal\n  `boom`, diag `[[256 boom]]`, status 255).\n  [programs_p5b2.cljc](test/yang/php/antlr/programs_p5b2.cljc)\n\n### 2. Stream P2 (lower.cljc, e2e/portable/linked harnesses, prelude.cljc)\n\n- `lower/option-keys` drops `:request` and `lower/lower-program` drops the\n  request operand data: it takes an opaque `:request-node` (a UAST node,\n  defaulting to the `:php/null` literal) and splices it as `run-main`'s\n  second operand. Lowering performs no `sexp->uast` conversion of request\n  data anymore — a `lower-program` call never embeds a request record,\n  with or without options.\n  [lower.cljc](src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc)\n- Each harness composes the operand at the composition level from the\n  stream-consumed record: new `request-node` helpers in\n  [e2e_harness.clj](test/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj) and\n  [portable_harness.cljc](test/yang/php/antlr/portable_harness.cljc)\n  (`u/sexp->uast` of the record, converted harness-side); the lowering\n  stage only ever sees the opaque `:request-node`.\n  [linked_harness.cljc](test/yang/php/antlr/linked_harness.cljc)\n  converts its `:request` opt the same way. `lower-through-stage` with a\n  request still consumes from the request stream BEFORE lowering, and\n  `run-lifecycle-raw` still returns the drained composition-supplied\n  response/diagnostic streams alongside the task value.\n- Header replacement is now interpreted from the appended commands, not\n  by deleting earlier records: `php/emit-header!` is append-only (every\n  emission is a `{header line :replace bool}` command) and the new\n  `php/response-view` fold applies replace semantics (case-insensitive\n  field-name match, status/cookie records pass through in order) at read\n  time in `run-main`'s result. Observable `:php/response` values are\n  unchanged (verified identical by the header fixtures).\n  [prelude.cljc](src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc)\n- Response and diagnostic emission happen DURING VM execution on the\n  composition-supplied streams: `run-lifecycle-raw` attaches both\n  stream handles to the walker VM\n  (`engine/attach-resource`, sealed under the task secret) and passes\n  the sealed references as `run-main`'s third and fourth operands\n  (`:response-node`/`:diag-node`, opaque like `:request-node`);\n  `php/emit-response!` and `php/warn-sink` `stream/put!` onto them\n  during the run, and the runtime no longer appends to `php.rt/response`\n  / `php.rt/diag` cells on this path. The `stream` module is registered\n  in both portable registries and `stream/put! stream/cursor\n  stream/poll!` join `host-names` (the `prelude-reaches-no-dao-host`\n  contract now admits the `stream` namespace). `run-main`'s result\n  drains each stream (fresh oldest cursor + `poll!` loop) and folds the\n  records through `php/response-view`; the body record is appended to\n  the stream before the read. The post-completion `emit-all!` copy is\n  deleted — with it gone and the gates still green, the records\n  provably arrived via in-VM `put!` during execution.\n  [prelude.cljc](src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc)\n  [portable_harness.cljc](test/yang/php/antlr/portable_harness.cljc)\n  [lower.cljc](src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc)\n- Compositions without streams are unchanged: e2e `run-raw`, linked runs\n  and `prelude-test` pass two operands (missing operands bind nil,\n  normalized to `:php/null`), so `php.rt/response-stream` /\n  `php.rt/diag-stream` stay null and the cells accumulate exactly as\n  before — `request-context` (which asserts `:response` on the\n  stream-less `run-raw`) is untouched. New maintained test\n  `:lowering-splices-stream-operands-test` pins the 4-operand splice\n  shape and the 2-operand default.\n\n### 3. HTTP/cookie residuals (prelude.cljc, programs_p5b2.cljc)\n\n- `http_response_code(0)` is a getter regardless of headers-sent: the\n  zero check moved ahead of the refusal check, so a post-output `(0)`\n  call answers the current code with no refusal diagnostic. Verified\n  against main.c/SAPI behavior (the 0Arg getter never touches headers).\n  New fixture `:http-response-code-zero-after-output-is-getter`.\n  [prelude.cljc](src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc)\n  [programs_p5b2.cljc](test/yang/php/antlr/programs_p5b2.cljc)\n- Cookie excess arguments throw `ArgumentCountError` (was `ValueError`),\n  with the exact PHP 8.3 wordings verified against php-src: positional\n  excess `setcookie() expects at most 7 arguments, N given`\n  (zend_API.c `zend_wrong_parameters_count_error`); array-form excess\n  `setcookie(): Expects exactly 3 arguments when argument #3\n  ($expires_or_options) is an array` (head.c `php_setcookie_common`,\n  capital E verbatim).\n  [prelude.cljc](src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc)\n- Unknown-option messages match head.c `php_head_parse_cookie_options_array`\n  verbatim: numeric key `setcookie(): option array cannot have numeric\n  keys`; unknown name `setcookie(): option \"bogus\" is invalid` (was\n  `Unknown option 'bogus'`). Both stay `ValueError`. The existing\n  unknown-option fixture text updated; new numeric-key fixture added.\n  [prelude.cljc](src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc)\n  [programs_p5b2.cljc](test/yang/php/antlr/programs_p5b2.cljc)\n- Array-option coercions restored per head.c (`zval_get_long` /\n  `zval_get_string` / `zval_is_true` per slot: expires→int,\n  path/domain/samesite→string, secure/httponly→bool) via new\n  `php/cookie-opt-value`; new `:setcookie-array-options-coerced` fixture\n  (`'1700003600'`→1700003600, `1`→true).\n  [prelude.cljc](src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc)\n\n### 4. Oracle runner (oracle.clj)\n\n- Plain-fatal parsing no longer populates both slots: the fatal branch\n  answers `:uncaught nil` and preserves the message as `:fatal` only.\n  [oracle.clj](src/dev/yang/php/oracle.clj)\n- The fold carries `:fatal` and the exit status: `print-fold` now prints\n  `{... :fatal :status}` with `:status` taken from the run's `:exit`.\n  [oracle.clj](src/dev/yang/php/oracle.clj)\n- The pending-fixture exclusion stays (`check-p5b2-fixture` still\n  requires a non-`:pending` oracle); the check already compares engine\n  `:fatal` and the shiva `:exit` against the fixture's `:fatal`/\n  `:status`, so the seat's shiva pass decides acceptance on the recorded\n  values. No change needed beyond the parser/fold fixes. Docker is\n  absent on this laptop, so the oracle pass itself was not run here.\n\n## Verification (laptop)\n\n- `clojure -M:test -n yang.php.antlr.p5b2-lifecycle-test\n  -n yang.php.antlr.request-context-test`: 8 tests / 188 assertions,\n  0 failures, 0 errors (the gate; includes the new\n  `lowering-splices-stream-operands-test`).\n- `clojure -M:test -n yang.php.antlr.prelude-test\n  -n yang.php.antlr.class-model-test\n  -n yang.php.antlr.lower-portable-test`: 49 tests / 2214 assertions,\n  0 failures, 0 errors.\n- `clojure -M:kondo` on all seven touched files: 0 errors, 0 warnings.\n- cljstyle not installed on this laptop (same as r2); edits follow\n  surrounding file style. Seat runs `cljstyle check`.\n- `e2e-test` cannot run on this laptop: missing generated\n  `yang.typescript.antlr.gen.TypeScriptLexer` (pre-existing environment\n  gap, unrelated to this change). `include-test` was started; outcome\n  below.\n- New fixtures are the maintained regression tests (durable-test\n  collateral): destructor suppression + status 255, getter-after-output,\n  ArgumentCountError (both forms), head.c option messages, option\n  coercions. They fail on the pre-fix code paths (new messages/status\n  pins have no pre-fix producer).\n- NOT run locally per gate: e2e / slow / subsystem, shiva oracle (the\n  seat relays its tally). All new/changed B2 fixtures stay\n  `:oracle :pending` for the shiva `php:8.3` pass, especially the exact\n  ArgumentCountError/head.c texts and the 255 status.\n8:lowering, see \"P3-b landing status\" below). P4 and P5 are complete; P6 is in\n11:verification remain part of its landing. The legacy `yang/php.cljc` frontend\n17:**P3-b landing status.** The program-level lowering of the P3 plan (steps S2 to\n40:- Not in this landing: the per-table iterator registry (C26, slice P3-c), the\n346:`Iterator`/`IteratorAggregate` objects; `ArrayAccess` and `Countable` are\n949:|    |                                    | `IteratorAggregate` dispatch per   |\n979:|    |                                    | propagate. `:ptr` is copied from h |\n1144:|    |                                    | propagates                         |\n1344:### 4.7 Oracle gates before landing\n1346:The final review's sign-off keeps the implementation oracle gates: each of\n1627:`Generator`, `Traversable`, `Iterator`, `IteratorAggregate`, `ArrayAccess`,\n1985:PHP depends on L1 to L4 (`yang.typescript.md` section 16) landing first. Every\n2441:lands**. After landing, a disagreement between a row and the pinned PHP CLI is\n2443:contradicts Zend blocks landing of any slice whose support profile includes\n2452:The landing gate is therefore: every claimed-row fixture equals the oracle;\n2501:13. (B8.13) The blocking rule of section 17.3 binding for `yang.php` landings\n2595:  corners. The stated implementation oracle gates remain required\" (section\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
