{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,65p' /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b2/src/dev/yang/php/oracle.clj; sed -n '1,85p' /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b2/test/yang/php/antlr/portable_harness.cljc; cat /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b2/test/yang/php/antlr/request_context_test.clj | head -70\"","aggregated_output":"(ns yang.php.oracle\n  \"PHP 8.3 CLI oracle runner for `yang.php.antlr.programs`\n   (docs/design/yang.php.md sections 14, 17.3).\n\n   For every fixture in `programs/fixtures` (plus `matrix-source` and\n   `float-cases`), writes the PHP source to a temporary file and runs:\n     docker run --rm -v <dir>:/w -w /w php:8.3-cli php \\\\\n       -d display_errors=1 -d html_errors=0 -d error_reporting=E_ALL \\\\\n       -d log_errors=0 <file>\n   Parses stdout into `:out`, `:diag` (`[[errno message] ...]`) and `:uncaught`\n   (`{:class c :message m}`), and compares against each fixture's expectation\n   (or `:departure/:zend` for departure fixtures).\"\n  (:require\n    [clojure.java.io :as io]\n    [clojure.java.shell :as sh]\n    [clojure.string :as str]\n    [yang.php.antlr.programs :as programs]\n    [yang.php.antlr.programs-p3b :as p3b]\n    [yang.php.antlr.programs-p4 :as p4]\n    [yang.php.antlr.programs-p5 :as p5]\n    [yang.php.antlr.programs-p5b2 :as p5b2]\n    [yang.php.antlr.programs-p6 :as p6])\n  (:import\n    (java.nio.charset\n      StandardCharsets)\n    (java.nio.file\n      Files)\n    (java.nio.file.attribute\n      FileAttribute)))\n\n\n(def banner\n  \"The pinned PHP 8.3 CLI oracle provenance banner.\"\n  p3b/banner)\n\n\n(def p5-banner\n  \"The P5 request-context run's own provenance banner (version/host/date of\n  the P5 recording pass, not P3-b's).\"\n  \"php-8.3.35 shiva 2026-10-25\")\n\n\n(def ^:private errno-of\n  {\"Warning\" 2,\n   \"Notice\" 8,\n   \"Deprecated\" 8192,\n   \"Fatal error\" 1})\n\n\n(defn class-derived?\n  \"Whether the recorded diag entry carries a class-derived errno: the runner\n  parses only the `Warning|Notice|...` kind line, so the recorded number is\n  derived from the message class, not the true constant (e.g. `Notice` parses\n  to 8 where the engine's semantic truth for `E_USER_NOTICE` is 1024).\"\n  [diag-entry]\n  (boolean (:yang.php.oracle/class-derived (meta diag-entry))))\n\n\n(defn- mark-class-derived\n  \"Mark a recorded `[errno message]` pair as class-derived (see [[class-derived?]]).\"\n  [pair]\n  (with-meta pair {:yang.php.oracle/class-derived true}))\n\n\n(defn errno-match?\n(ns yang.php.antlr.portable-harness\n  \"What the JVM, Node and Dart lanes share: the host composition the PHP\n   profile runs over, the `packet` helper that builds a CST packet from a\n   nested form, and a parserless run of a packet on the AST walker.\"\n  (:require\n    [dao.stream :as stream]\n    [dao.stream.memory-log :as memory-log]\n    [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ringbuffer]\n    [yang.core.uast :as u]\n    [yang.php.antlr.lower :as lower]\n    [yang.php.antlr.prelude :as prelude]\n    [yin.vm :as vm]\n    [yin.vm.ast-walker :as ast-walker]\n    [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n    [yin.vm.data :as data]\n    [yin.vm.integer :as integer]\n    [yin.vm.module :as module]))\n\n\n(def ^:private capability-secret \"yin.vm.test-utils/capability-secret\")\n\n\n(defn make-stream\n  \"The composition's stream constructor: a deterministic ring buffer, answering\n   the create outcome the engine consumes. The lifecycle streams below come\n   from this same constructor, so request consumption and response/diagnostic\n   emission travel composition-supplied streams rather than vectors.\"\n  ([] (make-stream nil))\n  ([capacity]\n   (ringbuffer/create!\n     {:dao.stream/type ringbuffer/transport-type,\n      ringbuffer/capacity-key (or capacity vm/default-stream-capacity)})))\n\n\n(defn- check-ok!\n  [result what]\n  (when-not (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome result))\n    (throw (ex-info (str \"PHP lifecycle stream failed: \" what) {:result result})))\n  result)\n\n\n(defn- lifecycle-stream\n  \"One open lifecycle stream handle from the composition's own constructor.\"\n  [what]\n  (:dao.stream/handle (check-ok! (make-stream) what)))\n\n\n(defn create-vm\n  \"An AST walker composed with the harness's deterministic ring-buffer stream.\"\n  ([] (create-vm {}))\n  ([opts]\n   (ast-walker/create-vm\n     (merge {:make-stream (fn [capacity] (make-stream capacity)),\n             :capability-secret capability-secret}\n            opts))))\n\n\n(defn- new-memory-log\n  []\n  (let [result (memory-log/create! {:dao.stream/type memory-log/transport-type})]\n    (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome result))\n      (:dao.stream/handle result)\n      (throw (ex-info \"PHP harness memory-log creation failed\" {:result result})))))\n\n\n(defn- drain\n  [handle]\n  (let [start (get-in (stream/cursor handle stream/anchor-oldest)\n                      [:dao.stream/cursor])]\n    (loop [cursor start, acc []]\n      (let [result (stream/next handle cursor)]\n        (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome result))\n          (recur (:dao.stream/cursor result)\n                 (conj acc (:dao.stream/value result)))\n          acc)))))\n\n\n(def integer-limits\n  \"The `integer` limits the PHP compositions here install.\"\n  {::integer/max-bits 100000, ::integer/max-digits 4300})\n\n\n(def data-limits {::data/max-items 1048576})\n\n\n(ns yang.php.antlr.request-context-test\n  \"P5 request records, response records, output buffering and isolation.\"\n  (:require\n    [clojure.string :as str]\n    [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n    [yang.php.antlr.e2e-harness :as h]\n    [yang.php.antlr.programs-p5 :as p5]))\n\n\n(defn- diagnostics\n  [r]\n  (mapv (juxt :errno :message) (:php/diag r)))\n\n\n(defn- strip-output-started\n  \"Strip the oracle's location suffix ` by (output started at ...)` from a\n  recorded diagnostic message (the headers-already-sent ruling: the engine\n  records the bare refusal text).\"\n  [msg]\n  (str/replace msg #\" by \\(output started at .*\\)$\" \"\"))\n\n\n(defn- normalize-expected-diag\n  \"Normalize the fixture (oracle-fold) `:diag` before comparing against the\n  engine: the oracle's location suffix is stripped from headers-already-sent\n  texts (the engine records the bare refusal text per the headers ruling).\n  The empty-`ob_end_clean` notice the oracle records is kept verbatim — the\n  engine emits it per the notice ruling. Fold records stay verbatim.\"\n  [expected-diag]\n  (mapv (fn [[errno msg]] [errno (strip-output-started msg)])\n        expected-diag))\n\n\n(deftest request-binding-smoke-test\n  (is (= \"1\" (:php/out (h/run-raw \"<?php echo 1;\" {})))))\n\n\n(deftest request-context-fixtures-test\n  (doseq [{:keys [id source request out diag response status]} p5/fixtures]\n    (testing (name id)\n      (let [r (h/run-raw source request)]\n        (is (= out (:php/out r)))\n        (is (= (normalize-expected-diag (vec diag)) (diagnostics r)))\n        (when response (is (= response (:php/response r))))\n        (when status (is (= status (:php/status r))))\n        (is (nil? (:php/uncaught r)))))))\n\n\n(deftest requests-in-separate-tasks-share-nothing-test\n  (let [source (str \"<?php header('X-Request: ' . $_GET['value']);\"\n                    \" echo $_GET['value']; $_GET['value'] = 'changed';\")\n        request-a (assoc p5/request :php.request/query (p5/request-array [[\"value\" \"A\"]]))\n        request-b (assoc p5/request :php.request/query (p5/request-array [[\"value\" \"B\"]]))\n        a (h/run-raw source request-a)\n        b (h/run-raw source request-b)]\n    (is (= \"A\" (:php/out a)))\n    (is (= \"B\" (:php/out b)))\n    (is (= [{:php.response/header \"X-Request: A\", :replace true}\n            {:php.response/body \"A\"}]\n           (:php/response a)))\n    (is (= [{:php.response/header \"X-Request: B\", :replace true}\n            {:php.response/body \"B\"}]\n           (:php/response b)))\n    (is (empty? (:php/diag a)))\n    (is (empty? (:php/diag b)))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
